## 12. Things that will trip up a new engineer (stated as facts)

- The `{ units }` "primary path" / "TCS Python pipeline" wording in the code and
  OpenAPI spec vs. `CLAUDE.md`'s record that the integration is inactive — the
  `{ text }` / `runPipeline` path is the one that runs (§6).
- `test-results.json` is both committed to the repo and uploaded as an artifact by
  `run-tests` — two copies of the same state.
- The workflow list shows more workflows than there are workflow files on the branch
  (§9 caveat).
- Several temporary diagnostic files are currently present on `main` (§9).
- The five system-harness checks verify form and source-traceability, not meaning
  correctness (§8a). Meaning correctness is checked only by the rule harnesses on
  curated cases (§8b).
- Documentation convention: `README.md`, `DESIGN.md`, `TESTING.md`, and other `.md`
  files are changed only in a dedicated documentation pass, not as a side effect of a
  build/fix. `CLAUDE.md` is the exception that may be updated during build work.
